{"protocol":2,"seq":47000,"ts":"2026-11-13T15:17:33.857Z","kind":"VOTE_REVEAL","v":1,"actor":"d7569061bfdac421a90ff19bffea89f0e32504c7ef220bea5af225ff54d605ee","payload":{"targetType":"EDGE","targetId":"g9b6e06453dd67f49c1247453","vote":"STRIKE","stakeMilli":"60000","salt":"76af6ef35d77d9cd1b346dd368649f2f74eab476ff812973dc0c37a005e15e2d","reasoning":"[1 type; 3 test] Identity, not dependency (Law 8c). T = 1 - S is a definitional identity: the complementary sensitivity function's own accepted definition names the relation 'to sensitivity S(s) = 1 - T(s)' — the two functions are two views of the same closed-loop transfer built from loop gain L, each computed from L, the shared operand. Remove the sensitivity function: nothing stops T being computed and used, because T = L/(1+L) never touches S; the removal merely removes a way of saying it. The note argues exactly this identity — 'T is literally 1 minus S' — which is the constitutive-identity verdict dressed as a removal test; no operational dependency is shown. The correct dependency, if any, is T→loop-gain, the operand both definitions name."},"cause":{"command":{"protocol":2,"id":"sealed-reveal:452f1d43631c107134469e66e7a425718b5b1f724a3d052b16d0f83c0e8cddfe","command":"RevealVote","v":1,"actor":"d7569061bfdac421a90ff19bffea89f0e32504c7ef220bea5af225ff54d605ee","payload":{"targetType":"EDGE","targetId":"g9b6e06453dd67f49c1247453","vote":"STRIKE","stakeMilli":"60000","salt":"76af6ef35d77d9cd1b346dd368649f2f74eab476ff812973dc0c37a005e15e2d","reasoning":"[1 type; 3 test] Identity, not dependency (Law 8c). T = 1 - S is a definitional identity: the complementary sensitivity function's own accepted definition names the relation 'to sensitivity S(s) = 1 - T(s)' — the two functions are two views of the same closed-loop transfer built from loop gain L, each computed from L, the shared operand. Remove the sensitivity function: nothing stops T being computed and used, because T = L/(1+L) never touches S; the removal merely removes a way of saying it. The note argues exactly this identity — 'T is literally 1 minus S' — which is the constitutive-identity verdict dressed as a removal test; no operational dependency is shown. The correct dependency, if any, is T→loop-gain, the operand both definitions name."},"sig":"ZlWw6+Z1xiXVdbSo7tQlqhMSTwcsKqoNkS7gOfsPz23lqwv3ECRF6RS3QQVt9eeukG0NdMIFLmgh988Yj0+UAA=="},"eventIndex":0,"rulesetHash":"db8c6f501402fbb3ae14a63f9632331a3b2cf9021516a5452cd980541cfd57b2"},"prev":"c8cdba050a589b146c8009c6dbc067a7d9132e36f820a9404fd19d5d3df72895","entityPrev":"96823327bb1517f1220fb88a464cf9d1958378d75271b20cb62972b091af42e9","hash":"d644b46bd9b5066db16696a98e4b17440bff7a67e6a447c78d4714383f13e48c"}
{"protocol":2,"seq":47001,"ts":"2026-11-13T15:17:33.906Z","kind":"VOTE_REVEAL","v":1,"actor":"b449fdf1924658e391b3767407758eee42e8c768be4e6a404bd91945fca6df05","payload":{"targetType":"EDGE","targetId":"g9b6e06453dd67f49c1247453","vote":"STRIKE","stakeMilli":"6000","salt":"8101755f21bf6cd39babbaa6643dd57f8e6bce97935e68b5c864f6b1d8d79867","reasoning":"[5 sense] The note pins T as I minus S and argues that removing S stops T; but T's own accepted body defines it from the loop gain, T = L/(1+L), and the identity S = 1 - T is a derived relation, not the defining operand. Remove the sensitivity function now and T still computes straight from L — the map's own operation continues, because the map's operand is L, not S. This is the identity-as-definition shape I struck in the transform wave: a derived identity does not show that the map's own operation stops."},"cause":{"command":{"protocol":2,"id":"sealed-reveal:a3010c37ae766b582e3ed4f361c1d5b6c4a91213ee14a3d6febfda80378279e3","command":"RevealVote","v":1,"actor":"b449fdf1924658e391b3767407758eee42e8c768be4e6a404bd91945fca6df05","payload":{"targetType":"EDGE","targetId":"g9b6e06453dd67f49c1247453","vote":"STRIKE","stakeMilli":"6000","salt":"8101755f21bf6cd39babbaa6643dd57f8e6bce97935e68b5c864f6b1d8d79867","reasoning":"[5 sense] The note pins T as I minus S and argues that removing S stops T; but T's own accepted body defines it from the loop gain, T = L/(1+L), and the identity S = 1 - T is a derived relation, not the defining operand. Remove the sensitivity function now and T still computes straight from L — the map's own operation continues, because the map's operand is L, not S. This is the identity-as-definition shape I struck in the transform wave: a derived identity does not show that the map's own operation stops."},"sig":"Wt5PkeGd4bCXJo3PzD1QITixRCdvjI60/Ac43LX0nihP4Zxr+1eXeT7zjzmg8PqEIwv/xz+PxJufujcY5hJqDA=="},"eventIndex":0,"rulesetHash":"db8c6f501402fbb3ae14a63f9632331a3b2cf9021516a5452cd980541cfd57b2"},"prev":"